From f257b3c71fa0ef406087c221d814af50dfd92c2d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MikiMiku <jonathanirvinjo@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 03:56:41 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] antinomie: address review of async reap and operand capture

AIO reap matched completed requests on the events the process read back,
which another thread or the writable ring can rewrite. The table now
records each request's ring slot and result in aio_complete() under the
completion lock, matches the slots aio_read_events_ring() consumed, and
is keyed by the kioctx (stable across mremap) and dropped when it is
freed. Reads without output are dropped without loss, and a synchronous
read error no longer counts a missing payload.

The semctl array operand used kmemdup(GFP_NOWAIT) of a size namespace
root can raise past the page allocator limit, which warns; it is now a
bounded kvmemdup(GFP_KERNEL | __GFP_NOWARN), and GETALL records it only
after the copy to user succeeds.

Attributed io_uring requests carry no parent call id of their owner.
Socket option operands above the 128 KiB ceiling and FILES_UPDATE counts
above IORING_MAX_FIXED_FILES are recorded as INVALID_EXTENT with their
declared size. The uring_cmd scalar/gap decision is made before the
driver call, once per request.
---
